  "objects": [
    {
      "kind": "script",
      "x": 7,
      "y": 5,
      "text": [
        "A notice bolted to the first post, in Mirehaven paint on Emberfall iron.",
        "THE WALK IS THE ROAD. THE ROAD IS NOT THE GROUND.",
        "Under it, later and smaller: SPAN 9 IS STILL OUT. IT HAS BEEN THREE YEARS."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "script",
      "x": 18,
      "y": 10,
      "text": [
        "POST 4. The board is new. The post it is nailed to is not.",
        "Somebody has cut a tally of forty-one marks down the side of it.",
        "The last eleven are in a different hand and they are further apart."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "script",
      "x": 29,
      "y": 12,
      "text": [
        "POST 5, at the far corner of the loop, and a bench nobody maintains.",
        "From here you can hear the fog bell and not see the Waystation at all.",
        "That is the arrangement. You walk at the sound."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "script",
      "x": 12,
      "y": 18,
      "text": [
        "POST 6, and the fog bell hung off it: cast in Emberfall, carried out here",
        "on two poles by four people who all still mention it.",
        "Rung at dusk, and again whenever anybody is late."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "script",
      "x": 18,
      "y": 29,
      "text": [
        "POST 9. Below the number, painted over twice and legible through both:",
        "SPAN OUT. WADE OR GO ROUND. THE ROUND WAY IS LONGER AND YOU WILL LIVE.",
        "Somebody has added in charcoal: THE WADE IS FINE. And under that: IT IS NOT."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "script",
      "x": 32,
      "y": 37,
      "text": [
        "POST 12, and a stack of sawn piles beside it under a tarpaulin.",
        "This is not Mirehaven timber. Every end is stamped with a circle and a line,",
        "and the delivery note is made out to a survey, not to a town."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "script",
      "x": 32,
      "y": 46,
      "text": [
        "POST 14. From here the lanterns run the whole way in, four apart,",
        "and somebody walks out every evening and lights every one of them.",
        "That is the entire reason anyone arrives at Mirehaven alive."
      ]
    },
